"prose": [
{
"from": 159,
"to": 160,
"text": "These are the standing lint and unit entries. The Windows-target clippy reads `stop.rs`'s `cfg(windows)` routine and its case on the Linux host, check only. G1 and the lint probes run."
},
{
"from": 162,
"to": 165,
"text": "Three integration binaries run: - `cli_verify`: the new stop table, plus every existing verify case, which holds the uninterrupted run byte-identical; - `cli_version_gate`: `run`'s gate over the changed `run_bounded`; - `contract_diag_schema`: the schema with the twelfth member."
},
{
"from": 167,
"to": 170,
"text": "A literal probe confirms the two moved literals are gone from product code. A preservation guard holds every other file; it reads no `Cargo.toml` or `Cargo.lock` change. `cargo deny`, the harness smoke with G2 and G4, and the native `pre-push` run. The operator pass fires hygiene, the push and the CI read (`leg = 'operator'`). The CI read is where the `cfg(windows)` unit case and the macOS leg are read."
},
{
"from": 172,
"to": 174,
"text": "The criteria that name `ledger/stamps.json`, the run's dirs and `cli-<name>.ndjson` are asserted inside the step 8 cases, over each case's own test home, cwd and temp root, which the cases create and read themselves. No entry produces them as a file a later entry reads, so no entry carries `artifact`."
},
{
"from": 176,
"to": 179,
"text": "No mutation entry, no witness run and no workflow dispatch is listed (`inputs#I1`). No entry is a live leg. Nothing starts the real `claude`: the stop is proven against the fake agent, and the plan holds zero live starts (`inputs#I1`). The guards name their base `d9f01b1b8642`, HEAD at P4, because the operator pass's pre-CI commit moves HEAD onto the chunk."
}
],
